#Bullet cores & components
ie.manual.entry.bullet_cores.name=Bullet Cores
ie.manual.entry.bullet_cores.subtext=That one bounced!

ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_brass=Brass Core
ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_brass.lore=Make it Steampunk
ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_brass.desc=Brass is a heavy metal with bad penetration capabilities, but it greatly increases the effect of other components.

ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_copper=Copper Core
ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_copper.lore=Every Penny Counts
ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_copper.desc=Copper is a cheap material for bullets, its penetration ability is worse than one of brass, but its component effect.

ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_lead=Lead Core
ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_lead.lore=Good, bad and ugly
ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_lead.desc=Lead is a good material for cheap bullets with high damage and mediocre penetrating power, however due to its high density limits the maximum range of projectiles made of it.

ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_iron=Iron Core
ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_iron.lore=The Middle Class
ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_iron.desc=Iron is a good early material for bullets, it offers above-average penetrating power and range, but has weak component effect and damage.

ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_steel=Steel Core
ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_steel.lore=Full Metal Jacket
ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_steel.desc=Using steel is a non-expensive way to increase the penetration capabilties of the projectiles, only disadvantage is slightly decreased component effect.

ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_tungsten=Tungsten Core
ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_tungsten.lore=Load APCR!
ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_tungsten.desc=Tungsten is a better at penetrating objects than steel, but it decreases the effect of other components

ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_uranium=Uranium Core
ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_uranium.lore=What do you mean, ammo is depleted?
ie.manual.entry.bullet_core.core_uranium.desc=Low weight and hardness make uranium a great penetrator without loosing capability to carry explosive materials. Great, but expensive choice.

ie.manual.entry.bullet_components.name=Bullet Components
ie.manual.entry.bullet_components.subtext=Load APCRHEFSPTSD B-Capped!
ie.manual.entry.bullet_components.dmg_mod=Damage: %sx
ie.manual.entry.bullet_components.pen_mod=Penetration: %s vBH
ie.manual.entry.bullet_components.blast_mod=Blast Radius: %sx
ie.manual.entry.bullet_components.density=Density: %s
ie.manual.entry.bullet_components.type=Type: %s

#A quote from World in Conflict
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.firework=Fireworks
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.firework.lore=And now, free the skies
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.firework.desc=Fireworks, while mostly known for their beautiful looks, can be used to suppress and blind enemies.

#Quote from Company of Heroes/Market Garden campaign
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.tracer_powder=Tracer Powder
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.tracer_powder.lore=Fill the sky with tracers!
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.tracer_powder.desc=Tracers are a good way to see which way your bullet flies, this can be used for purely decorative purposes or for correcting a gun's shot angle.

#Reference to Codename Panzers: Cold War
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.flare_powder=Flare Powder
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.flare_powder.lore=Night became Day
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.flare_powder.desc=Flares can be used for illuminating or marking positions, this can be useful in directing artillery

#Reference to the book "Thus Spoke Zarathustra"
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.propaganda=Propaganda
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.propaganda.lore=He who obeys, does not listen to himself!
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.propaganda.desc=Propaganda can be used to instill fear in your enemies, that is if they can read, obviously.

#Fallout reference
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.nuke=Nuke
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.nuke.lore=War Never Changes
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.nuke.desc=Nuclear Explosives are the most powerful and destructive known to man, only thick layers of reinforced concrete can protect against its force. Moreover, heat caused by it melts down enemies around and even if they survive that, they will die of radiation quickly.

#Reference to a song
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.tnt=TNT
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.tnt.lore=Tons of it!
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.tnt.desc=TNT is an explosive material with mediocre destructive power. Because of how easy it is to produce, it is a good choice for machinegun bullets and grenades.

#CoH2 Reference
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.rdx=RDX
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.rdx.lore=Things go up, things go down!
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.rdx.desc=RDX, also known as the §shexogen§r is a powerful high-explosive material. Being twice as powerful as TNT and it's able to destroy even the heaviest emplacements.

#There are many variants of HMX's full name, one of them is Her Majesty's Explosive
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.hmx=HMX
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.hmx.lore=Her Majesty's Finest
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.hmx.desc=HMX is one of the most powerful conventional explosives, it's three times more powerful than TNT it's capable of breaching trough any fortifications.

#Reference to a song
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.white_phosphorus=White Phosphorus
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.white_phosphorus.lore=Storm clouds, fire and steel.
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.white_phosphorus.desc=White phosphorus is the main ingredient of most incendiary shells. Its high heat makes surrounding enemies more flammable, while the burning hot fragments ignite everything around.

#A reference to struggle between Tesla and Edison
#similar to how the Finns made a cocktail for Molotov (soviet foreign affairs minister) during the Winter War, a tesla grenade would be a nice one for Edison
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.tesla=Discharge Emitters
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.tesla.lore=A gift for Edison
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.tesla.desc=Discharge emitters create a field which disrupts the flow of electricity. They are useful in disabling industrial equipment, emplacements and sabotaging energy production.


ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_aluminum=Aluminum Shrapnel
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_aluminum.lore=Amelinium, one does not simply paint it
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_aluminum.desc=Aluminum is not the best material for shrapnel, but it's cheap enough to be mass used in combat.

ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_zinc=Zinc Shrapnel
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_zinc.lore=Better than tin!
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_zinc.desc=Zinc is not a good shrapnel material, but when there are shortages, anything will do.

#Reference to Terraria's coin gun
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_copper=Copper Shrapnel
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_copper.lore=Make coins your ammo
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_copper.desc=While throwing copper at the enemies won't bribe them, after a few shots it might make them dead.

#Reference to JoJo, yes even in the II there has to be one
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_platinum=Platinum Shrapnel
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_platinum.lore=A Shrapnel User, huh?
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_platinum.desc=Choosing Platinum? Yes, definitely, make yourself poor, you want it, not me.

#Murica' fuck yeah
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_gold=Gold Shrapnel
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_gold.lore=And who cares about Taxpayers?
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_gold.desc=Ah yes, the good old way of wasting money - war. While the bullets are somewhat expensive, they don't seem to have much effect on the opponent.

ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_nickel=Nickel Shrapnel
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_nickel.lore=Nickels and dimes
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_nickel.desc=Nickel is a bad choice for shrapnel, it doesn't deal much damage, but in hard times it can save the day.

#Reference to the Netflix's Witcher series
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_silver=Silver Shrapnel
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_silver.lore=Toss a coin to your gunner
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_silver.desc=Silver shrapnel is a good option for combating undead enemies, the shrapnel deals more damage to them and slows them down.

ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_electrum=Electrum Shrapnel
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_electrum.lore=The Shock Troops have arrived
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_electrum.desc=Electrum excels at conducting electricity, while the shapnel won't hurt much, enemies hit will receive more damage from energy weapons, such as tesla coils.

#Reference to a post-ww2 poster for inter-country help in Western Europe
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_constantan=Constantan Shrapnel
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_constantan.lore=<br>Whatever the weather, we kill enemies together.
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_constantan.desc=Constantan is well known for its heat conductive properties, enemies hit will be prone to fire damage for some time.

#Reference to words by Otto von Bismarck
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_iron=Iron Shrapnel
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_iron.lore=With Blood and Iron!
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_iron.desc=Iron is a good choice for shrapnel, it easily penetrates enemies wearing light armor.

ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_lead=Lead Shrapnel
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_lead.lore=Let the Lead rain!
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_lead.desc=Lead is a good shrapnel material, it's heavy and inflicts high damage on unarmored enemies.

#Japanese "hagane" means steel, but the literal translation is "full metal", Hagane no Renkinjutsushi
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_steel=Steel Shrapnel
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_steel.lore=The fullmetal in all its glory
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_steel.desc=Steel is a fine shrapnel material, good damage, scatter and speed make it effective against all opponents.

ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_brass=Brass Shrapnel
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_brass.lore=Ornamental Design
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_brass.desc=Brass is a bad choice for making shrapnel, although its high weight makes it deal more damage than other weak metals.

#A reference to Bear989sr. - a gregtech player, I just love when he says the word "steel", also some nice GT tutorials
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_tungsten=Tungsten Shrapnel
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_tungsten.lore=And now we make *ekhem* TUNGSTEN-STEEL...
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_tungsten.desc=Tungsten is a very good material for shrapnel, its high damage allows to shred enemies to pieces.

#Reference to Kuruma saying IEn's thorium railgun rods are the strongest railgun ammo
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_thorium=Thorium Shrapnel
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_thorium.lore=Make grenades, not rods!
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_thorium.desc=Thorium is a good, but costly shrapnel material with high damage and penetration values.

ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_HOPGraphite=HOP Graphite Shrapnel
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_HOPGraphite.lore=HOP to it!
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_HOPGraphite.desc=Graphite is a very good shrapnel material, its low weight and high piercing capabilities make it useful in combat.

ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_uranium=Uranium Shrapnel
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_uranium.lore=Ra-di-o-active
ie.manual.entry.bullet_component.shrapnel_uranium.desc=Uranium is one of the best materials for shrapnel, the scattering fragments have no problem piercing trough armor and can deal high damage to any target.
